{"title":"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_20\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 20</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Common_sense)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Common sense)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Modular_Arithmetic)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Modular Arithmetic)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(pretty_braindead)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (pretty braindead)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_20\">Problem 20</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 20\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab9fc2533c4c85549baa0fd13ca1d94e7b03cd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1,2,3,...,19\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"18\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/3/c735d6a627b91150d3ebdeae431fc2f86df26b28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b \\in S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"16\" />, define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/f/a3f681ed361802f316f3fd5db54858dbf51778e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\succ b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> to mean that either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f50ae347f36db34352cee98e1521350c7a6d944c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; a - b \\le 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/0/32061883d061a38ad81813ee8ef09cecd1c7e978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b - a &gt; 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"72\" height=\"13\" />. How many ordered triples <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/3/c73ed093cc73a8d9a14185fa525e7067e5c3725d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y,z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> of elements of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> have the property that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/7/8e73253016df5627fefc1396ed238bfb394c8b30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\succ y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/5/7b5bef0304989fa381a6e87ce2b36a4127911256.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y \\succ z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/1/521207eb6f4c6d36d3e4022afc80904754ac8616.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z \\succ x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"11\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/8/028235c384d01d8f5dea69cfa2da85ab5ecc289f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)} \\ 810 \\qquad  \\textbf{(B)} \\ 855 \\qquad  \\textbf{(C)} \\ 900 \\qquad  \\textbf{(D)} \\ 950 \\qquad  \\textbf{(E)} \\ 988$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"439\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Imagine that the 19 numbers are just 19 persons sitting evenly around a circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />; each of them is facing to the center. \n</p><p>One may check that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/7/8e73253016df5627fefc1396ed238bfb394c8b30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\succ y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is one of the 9 persons on the left of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/8/aa866dc31ff99cac53235df5545377e6a280bf1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y \\succ x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is one of the 9 persons on the right of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. Therefore, \"<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/7/8e73253016df5627fefc1396ed238bfb394c8b30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\succ y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/5/7b5bef0304989fa381a6e87ce2b36a4127911256.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y \\succ z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/1/521207eb6f4c6d36d3e4022afc80904754ac8616.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z \\succ x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"11\" />\" implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/0/d20258310be3455daf8318274224a9d1d28fb6a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y, z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"11\" /> cuts the circumference of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> into three arcs, each of which has no more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> numbers sitting on it (inclusive).\n</p><p>We count the complement: where the cut generated by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/3/c73ed093cc73a8d9a14185fa525e7067e5c3725d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y,z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> has ONE arc that has more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> persons sitting on. Note that there can only be one such arc because there are only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbfe273946ff9f971c5eab331ca39caa6fdf7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> persons in total.\n</p><p>Suppose the number of persons on the longest arc is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/0/110330a0a87f802d3610749d57f1afaf5a09ec69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&gt;10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />. Then two places of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accc80fdf164cef264f56a82b6f9f6add320fe05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> are just chosen from the two end-points of the arc, and there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/f/ccf5ae774ea982fc8f16b40db23c3902dec83f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19-k$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"13\" /> possible places for the third person. Once the three places of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accc80fdf164cef264f56a82b6f9f6add320fe05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> are chosen, there are three possible ways to put <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accc80fdf164cef264f56a82b6f9f6add320fe05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> into them clockwise. Also, note that for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/0/110330a0a87f802d3610749d57f1afaf5a09ec69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&gt;10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbfe273946ff9f971c5eab331ca39caa6fdf7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> ways to choose an arc of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore the total number of ways (of the complement) is \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/e/25efcaa790c44863401a29b60bc04a11d1aea380.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=11}^{18} 3\\cdot 19 \\cdot (19-k) = 3\\cdot 19 \\cdot (1+\\cdots+8) = 3\\cdot 19\\cdot 36\\]\" width=\"422\" height=\"50\" />\n</p><p>So the answer is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/0/d20bc97c03ec0038ec40124df805e17d3b337d92.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3\\cdot \\binom{19}{3} - 3\\cdot 19\\cdot 36 = 3\\cdot 19 \\cdot (51 - 36) = 855\\]\" width=\"363\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>NOTE: this multiple-choice problem can be done even faster -- after we realized the fact that each choice of the three places of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accc80fdf164cef264f56a82b6f9f6add320fe05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> corresponds to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible ways to put them in, and that each arc of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/0/110330a0a87f802d3610749d57f1afaf5a09ec69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&gt;10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbfe273946ff9f971c5eab331ca39caa6fdf7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> equitable positions, it is evident that the answer should be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/a/25a1d2b26247509c01ec4eb41ea3b3c775353ce1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\cdot 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"39\" height=\"13\" />,  which can only be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/d/b7d05977e249669c8458358830f45ae647f965f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$855$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> from the five choices.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we can find out that the only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/0/d20258310be3455daf8318274224a9d1d28fb6a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y, z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"11\" /> that satisfy the conditions in the problem are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad5e4d30650280d29f016aae71d61e811467690.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1 \\leq z-y \\leq 9 , 1 \\leq y-x \\leq 9 , z-x \\geq 10)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"329\" height=\"18\" /> , <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78df151a1b303b8ec4e49fbb325860b7e4cb4e98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1 \\leq y-x \\leq 9 , 1 \\leq x-z \\leq 9 , y-z \\geq 10)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"329\" height=\"18\" /> , and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/0/720728c3ec76cc4c81ae02c86e5f310d9b8ce7bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1 \\leq x-z \\leq 9 , 1 \\leq z-y \\leq 9 , x-y \\geq 10)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"329\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>Consider the 1st set of conditions for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/0/d20258310be3455daf8318274224a9d1d28fb6a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y, z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"11\" />. We get that there are\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/3/b932a212472a23e42428ac119b9d85896a9e76e7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[45\\cdot 10 - \\sum_{k=1}^{9} \\binom{k+1}{2} = 285\\]\" width=\"220\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>cases for the first set of conditions.\n</p><p>Since the 2nd and 3rd set of conditions are simply rotations of the 1st set, the total number of cases is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/4/7d4d990cddcf4707a4ac2ff8aded51d856e145b7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3\\cdot 285 = \\fbox{(B)855}\\]\" width=\"134\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Common_sense.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Common_sense)\">Solution 3 (Common sense)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Common sense)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The conditions are very strange. The major way <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accc80fdf164cef264f56a82b6f9f6add320fe05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> can satisfy is if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad5e4d30650280d29f016aae71d61e811467690.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1 \\leq z-y \\leq 9 , 1 \\leq y-x \\leq 9 , z-x \\geq 10)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"329\" height=\"18\" /> because at this point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1e262a6265f07a0e2dc67de73372358de2b376.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z &gt; x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"10\" /> no matter what. This is the only case that works, but we can rotate the variables around, so our answer is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/6/856b07fabfe93b03653554acf31defe3500563b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=y+a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/1/a319b62ffbc383f8d4a9dcf9cc46107148b55617.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/4/864304045cc8c5b72a995ced6426e7b6d907ff13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;a,b&lt;10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" />. That means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/5/c4535eeda85c95b1dfbab4ffe039f510609db42a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=x+a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"108\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/e/3be23036c7f28e9edf8d435c5799dc277885a7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 \\leq z \\leq 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"96\" height=\"16\" />. WLOG <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/3/cd339101328450e720240e07a4b7c17f21d99a2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z&gt;y&gt;x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"15\" />. \nStart casework on what <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> is, anywhere from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. There are 2 main factors:\n1. the number of ways to choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9bdf3e496517e8f8742f81dd774be1f93cf6e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/3/2433b45f309883be223f2a0f0391d7f22eb9ab6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"70\" height=\"14\" />.\n2. the number of ways to choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> or start the sequence, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/d/fcdb2ff508ae76be1f2a97d5b5d80ccc8f77c63d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19-(a+b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"96\" height=\"20\" />\nThe sum of all cases turns out to be the sum of squares from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/f/d7ff7fb175cc5bcf2b3253037e5e8b0cd466f64e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9^2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/1/c716d1dc907ae6b51cb0f545664c89d58b6b67d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/8/cc841173485aedb106ebfdce2de8c0827710de89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9 \\cdot 10 \\cdot 19}{2 \\cdot 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"78\" height=\"38\" />.\nMultiply that by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/9/87914f67b566bfacbb6457a12beb3c38dc0bda63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{(B)855}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"63\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~dragnin\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Modular_Arithmetic.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Modular_Arithmetic)\">Solution 4 (Modular Arithmetic)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Modular Arithmetic)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that if we take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/2/2329e29b4246a3c555ee4d00fcf11bd732187160.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c\\mod{19}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"18\" />, the conditions are equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/5/8555d85700b33e2e07a00c4036ab01603fa84703.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;a-b\\le{9}\\mod{19}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"179\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/5/785a5d6b1409890d32fbc8a4e6f174f1a6797441.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;b-c\\le{9}\\mod{19}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"178\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/b/21b64d42c68d87949169bd7c5d9e2da533eb6f6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;c-a\\le{9}\\mod{19}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"179\" height=\"17\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/5/235db93c31f9373978b968b663ad4c5b86b9ef73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=a-b, n=b-c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"163\" height=\"18\" />. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbfe273946ff9f971c5eab331ca39caa6fdf7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> ways to pick <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87edbdda753b32453027dc7cab023c0743b6b243.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$81$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> cases in our sample space for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/5/6851ca945f78b10a85c14fc57fbaf75e69f57241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m, n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"34\" height=\"11\" />. Of these cases, only those where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/b/29b09a0f8664eee33c70b568594d1fe9f6bad057.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n&gt;9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"15\" /> will work. By stars and bars, this turns out to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/6/cc61bcd70dd08ca88b8f214b03d595ad1613d97a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{10}{2}=45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"88\" height=\"53\" />, hence the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/6/8f66be698fb88e4baa1c6244f4ff588af5532e40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45*19=\\fbox{(B)855}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"140\" height=\"30\" />.\n~sigmapie\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28pretty_braindead.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(pretty_braindead)\">Solution 5 (pretty braindead)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (pretty braindead)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c1eb9eef017cb03cde25f92a9a90a4eb2c1330.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\succ_1 y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> will denote the first inequality, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e396e4e0de1d6a53286439f571f414477574a21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\succ_2 y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> will denote the second.\n</p><p><br />\nWe soon see that we cannot have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/6/ed6f2c7ad042a3c0ce22097a9c72010ff845211a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\succ_1 y \\succ_1 z \\succ_1 x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"137\" height=\"15\" /> by adding the inequalities we obtain from them together, as it results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/2/3f2c077a4a5da8f1ae69e049d30c50903e19634d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nSimilarly, we can't have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/1/1b1b94167652e06d97130c8060703cd1c66c4991.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\succ_2 y \\succ_2 z \\succ_2 x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"137\" height=\"15\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/8/b38d65f1c8fd7e48b17f74a78bb978e89364d833.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\succ_2 y \\succ_2 z \\succ_1 x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"137\" height=\"15\" /> is also not possible by observing the inequalities.\n</p><p><br />\nThus, we only have to consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/2/8a20b2a2e802a9681d0ac0e1d797274cd0866f5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\succ_1 y\\succ_1 z \\succ_2 x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"137\" height=\"15\" />. Something like <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/e/a7e9d5c83be2d930ac6b90f80809624645aa9ff1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\succ_2 y \\succ_1 z \\succ_1 x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"137\" height=\"15\" /> is just a rotation of this case.\n</p><p><br />\nHere, we start with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/5/4655d5f2c9d5eb6fd66e36ea83293e6446363a5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;x-y\\le 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"111\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/8/fa8bc90d24b5666f4a6e8a1d184dcf9db5a02b5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;y-z\\le 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/5/d9594f310c30084a75b8c151a8c086c60a29b1a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-z &gt; 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" />. We begin with casework on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, since it is the smallest.\n</p><p><br />\nWhen <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/d/6bd3d68e77a39e1ea97e7009f70e12622fa76835.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> can range from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a057cb49277fe0c03b2240bc8f3f58552fa038f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[11,19]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" />. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/1/9012c15061efa06a9063c8a8114d2e9c1ad8f00b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9+8+7+6+5+4+3+2+1 = 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"301\" height=\"14\" /> different values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> as x ranges across <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/d/b4d14aad0671258cfff28162389216799fd507fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11-19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nWhen <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/6/5e6dc42bb0d892a136cd56c48b13585b42428825.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=2$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> can range from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/b/2cb9e406963e8d5acd8a3aa73ce9672f331478cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[12-19]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" />. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/3/863e98cbc59543dd8fe30dca8298c795acb3ee3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9+8+7+6+5+4+3+2 = 44$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"273\" height=\"15\" /> different values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> as x ranges across <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/c/d0c0a950ecc0a40cb749c90b43576db4ab15b989.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12-19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nContinuing this pattern, we get the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/4/2a455a58056aa0f6a873979c985f0b8703780ccd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45+44+42+39+35+30+24+17+9 = 285$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"386\" height=\"15\" />. Multiplying by three to count for rotations, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/c/20c6623a412abe4ab4ccb7bda16294bd9c7926c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(\\textbf{B}) 855}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"68\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p><p>-skibbysiggy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A\">2013 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017064917\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.056 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.077 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 661/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2298/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 20199/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.791      1 -total\n 58.77%    7.517      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 39.50%    5.052      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:11752:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017064917 and revision id 274483. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}